body:
We can make it not impact the production build by giving the errors in `if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development")`, which can be filtered out in webpack with either:

```js
new webpack.DefinePlugin({
  'process.env': {
    NODE_ENV: JSON.stringify('production')
  }
}),
```

or

```js
  new webpack.EnvironmentPlugin({
    NODE_ENV: 'development', // use 'development' unless process.env.NODE_ENV is defined
  }),
```

combined with uglify.

See as well how [react](https://facebook.github.io/react/docs/optimizing-performance.html#use-the-production-build) does it.
